<title>EGYPT: ENI agrees to help export Egyptian gas to Turkey.</title>
<headline>ENI agrees to help export Egyptian gas to Turkey.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt said on Wednesday the Italian state energy company ENI had agreed to take part in a project to export Egyptian gas to Turkey.</p>
<p>The Egyptian oil ministry said in the same statement that Egypt wanted the U.S. company Amoco to participate in the project. ENI and Amoco have been working closely in developing natural gas fields in and off the Nile Delta.</p>
<p>The statement did not say if the exports would be by pipeline or by tanker.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 489 0154/5</p>
</text>
